# C1-S02 — Stew. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1572–1624.
# Elara's house. The game slows down: the player can ask the basic questions
# here instead of having them dumped on the road. Each topic can be asked
# once. Inspectable objects have their own nodes.

~ start
do elara_serves_stew
Kaelen: This smells amazing. What is it?
Elara: Stew.
Kaelen: That's a category, not a recipe.
Elara: Today it's both. Eat it before it gets cold and turns into a different category.
=> topics

~ topics
? Kaelen (Internal): Ask her something?
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_where] So where am I, exactly? => where
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_fracture] What is the Fracture? => fracture
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_magic] How does magic work here? => magic
- [if not ch1_elara_arm_talked] About your arm... => arm
- (Just eat.) => END

~ where
set ch1_stew_asked_where
Elara: Aethelgard. You asked me that on the road.
Kaelen: I know. I'm asking again. Is that the country?
Elara: It's the world. All of it.
Kaelen: Of course it is. Why would it be anything smaller.
Elara: You did ask.
=> topics

~ fracture
set ch1_stew_asked_fracture
Elara: It's when things stop agreeing with themselves. Trees, water, roads. People, sometimes.
Kaelen: That's the actual definition?
Elara: It's the useful one. The priests have a longer one with more stars in it. It doesn't move carts.
=> topics

~ magic
set ch1_stew_asked_magic
Elara: You're asking me? You're the one who reached inside a beast this afternoon.
Kaelen: Okay. Point taken. I'll ask you again when I understand what I did.
=> topics

~ arm
set ch1_elara_arm_talked
[if elara_arm_respected_silence] => arm_waited
=> arm_pushed

~ arm_waited
Elara: You waited. On the road, when I did the cart. You saw, and you didn't say anything.
Kaelen: You didn't look like you wanted to talk about it.
Elara: I still don't.
Kaelen: Okay. Then we won't.
Elara: ...Thank you, stranger.
do trust elara 10
=> topics

~ arm_pushed
Elara: It's corruption. It's been there years. Every time I cast, it gets a little worse.
Kaelen: Then stop casting.
do pause 1.2
Elara: There it is.
Kaelen: There what is?
Elara: Stranger turns up, sees one afternoon of my life, and solves it.
Kaelen: I didn't mean it like that. I just—
Elara: I know you didn't. That's why I'm only annoyed with you.
=> topics

# ── Things in the room ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ inspect_bandages
Kaelen (Internal): Bandages. A lot of them, rolled and ready.
do elara_sees_him_look
Elara: They're mine, before you ask.
Kaelen: I guessed they might be.
Elara: Good. That saves us a conversation.

~ inspect_herbs
Kaelen (Internal): Half of these I don't recognise. The other half I don't recognise either.

~ inspect_focuses
Kaelen (Internal): Three cracked... wands? Foci? Whatever they are, she goes through them fast.

~ inspect_cloak
Kaelen (Internal): Patched so many times there's more patch than cloak.

~ inspect_map
Kaelen (Internal): Oakhaven, the crater, a road going south. Someone's drawn a skull over the north field.

# After the road ledger, on the way to her house.
~ invite
Elara: Come on, stranger. Food first, then you can worry about roads.
